  "strategy": "1. Approach and Rationale\nWe propose a hybrid optimization strategy combining genetic algorithms for global exploration with gradient-based methods for local refinement. The genetic algorithm efficiently explores the solution space, while gradient descent refines promising candidates, leveraging their complementary strengths to find an improved upper bound for C\u2085.\n\n2. Mathematical Specification\n- Variables: h \u2208 [0,1]^n, n=n_points, sum(h) = n/2.\n- Discretization: dx = 2.0 / n.\n- Objective: min_h max_k (convolve(h, 1-h, mode='full')[k] * dx)\n- Constraints: 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1 for all i, sum(h) = n/2.\n\n3. Implementation Procedure\na. Initialization:\n   - Population size P=100, max generations G=100.\n   - Initialize P random h vectors with 0.5 at n/2 positions, others 0.\nb. Genetic Algorithm Loop:\n   i. Evaluate C for each h in population.\n   ii. Select top 20% as parents.\n   iii. Crossover: Combine parents to create offspring by swapping segments.\n   iv. Mutate: Flip 5% of bits in offspring.\n   v. Replace bottom 20% in population with offspring.\nc. Gradient Refinement:\n   - Take top 10 h's, use scipy.optimize.minimize with constraints.\n   - Objective: C = max_k (convolutions).\nd. Validation:\n   - Ensure sum(h) = n/2, 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1.\n   - Compute exact C via evaluator.\n\n4. Search Choices and Variations\n- Population size P=100, Mutation rate 0.05, Crossover rate 0.8.\n- Gradient refinement on top 10% of population.\n- Use n_points=70 for efficiency, considering 1100s budget.\n\n5. Compute Budget and Robustness\n- Genetic algorithm: 600s.\n- Gradient descent: 500s.\n- Total: 1100s, including 100s overhead.\n\n6. Validation and Return Contract\n- Check feasibility: sum(h) = n/2, 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1.\n- Recompute C with evaluator to confirm accuracy.",
